{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/815305-prepared-for-anything-condition-vs-new-investigation-system","id":815305,"title":"\"Prepared for Anything\" Condition Vs. New Investigation System","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-24T01:03:57-08:00","id":815305,"title":"\"Prepared for Anything\" Condition Vs. New Investigation System","content":"So as Demon was written before the new core, it doesn't interact specifically with the new Investigations system. While it would be pretty trivial to plop in otherwise (and highly recommended, I'd say) I have some questions about how the Inquisitor's condition resolves vs. the Investigation system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prepared for Anything, Pg. 93 Demon The Descent</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resolution: The character can make a leap of logic, connecting disparate clues into a revelatory truth. Resolve this Condition to gain information from the Storyteller about how the current situation \u2014 how two plot threads tie together, what a good next step would be, or something that the character saw but just didn\u2019t connect until now. If no such element presents itself, the player can instead resolve this Condition to gain a +3 on any Mental Skill roll (Embeds and Exploits included).</div> </div> </div> </div>The line &quot;leap of logic&quot; makes me think that it could potentially be used to interact with the system in a few ways. Of course the secondary +3 could easily be resolved for an investigation roll, but that is less fun.<br /> <br /> My thoughts of the most obvious ones are:<br /> - Generate a new Clue when you don't have one.<br /> - Upgrade a Tainted or Incomplete Clue to a regular Clue<br /> - Reduced penalty for &quot;Uncovering the Truth&quot; when short of Clues.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if any of those are the &quot;correct&quot; use of the condition resolution (or if I've missed any other obvious points of interaction), so what do you guys think?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T03:33:32-08:00","id":815343,"title":"","content":"He said it best:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/aWuGbh.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}